item.description:
A surprise on California's beaches has scientists racing to give roughly 200 sea turtle eggs a fighting chance. An expedition is heading to a remote Pacific island to search for Amelia Earhart’s missing plane. A group of skydivers became heroes after spotting an emergency during a routine jump. What a day-in-the-life was like of a newly-minted Nobel Prize winner. Plus, Singapore is trying a new approach to get more people off their phones and start a reading habit.



Host/Producer: Krista Bo Polanco&nbsp;

Producer: Eryn Mathewson&nbsp;&nbsp;

Senior Producer: Felicia Patinkin&nbsp;

Editorial Support: Kathleen Magramo, Katie Hunt
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices

